# deploy-server environment file.
#
# Install as /root/secrets/deploy.env, root-owned, mode 0600. Created by hand
# over SSH; never committed, never in a deploy bundle:
#
#   install -m 600 /dev/null /root/secrets/deploy.env
#   vi /root/secrets/deploy.env
#
# Pulled in by the unit with EnvironmentFile=. Values are read literally by
# systemd -- no shell, no quotes needed, no expansion.

# --- auth-center (all three are REQUIRED) ---------------------------------
# There is no local key table and no legacy fallback: an instance missing any
# of these cannot authenticate anyone, so the server names the missing variable
# and exits instead of starting half-configured.

# Base URL of auth-center. NEVER hardcoded in the binary: do2 and dohl each get
# their own setting and their own service key so they revoke independently.
# The hostname is a deployment detail, so it is not written into this template.
DEPLOY_AUTH_URL=https://$AUTH_HOST

# This instance's own auth-center service key. Must hold `auth:introspect`.
# This is the secret that makes this file 0600.
DEPLOY_AUTH_KEY=

# The resource naming THIS INSTANCE's administration: do2-deploy on do2,
# dohl-deploy on dohl. `createProject` is checked against
# <this value>:create-project -- a scope is <resource>:<action>, two segments,
# action last, so the grouping lives in the resource NAME. The `-deploy` suffix
# is required: bare `do2` names the host, not its deploy service.
#
# There is deliberately no default and no derivation from the hostname, so an
# instance cannot fall back to something guessable. The requirements' config
# table omits this variable; it is a deliberate addition, because `createProject`
# resolves to no project and so has nothing else to be authorized against.
DEPLOY_ADMIN_RESOURCE=do2-deploy

# --- web dashboard (all three, or none) ------------------------------------
# The read-only dashboard: a browser page listing this instance's projects and
# what is live on each. Leave all three unset and the server simply does not
# serve one, which is the state every instance was in before it existed.
# Setting some but not all is a typo, and the server says so and exits.
#
# The dashboard is visibility only. A session is checked against
# <DEPLOY_ADMIN_RESOURCE>:admin-read and nothing else -- it cannot deploy, roll
# back, activate or run SQL. That is what makes it acceptable for it to depend
# on auth-center even though this server deploys auth-center: when that
# circular dependency bites, the CLI over SSH still does everything the
# dashboard could have.

# This server's own public origin, no trailing slash. The OAuth redirect URI is
# derived from it as <this>/oauth/callback and must match what auth-center has
# registered for the client, exactly.
#DEPLOY_PUBLIC_URL=https://deploy.example.com

# The SSO client registered in auth-center:
#   auth-setup create-sso-client "deploy dashboard" --project deploy \
#     --redirect-uri https://deploy.example.com/oauth/callback \
#     --post-logout-redirect-uri https://deploy.example.com/ \
#     --required-scope do2-deploy:admin-read
#DEPLOY_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=oc_...

# Shown once, when the client is registered. A second secret in this file.
#DEPLOY_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- storage (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# Overrides where db.sqlite lives. Unset on do2/dohl: running as root with
# neither this nor XDG_STATE_HOME set resolves to
# /root/.local/state/deploy/db.sqlite. Note this server does not migrate the
# old tool's schema — see "Cutover" in docs/server-setup.md. Only set this to
# move an instance.
#DEPLOY_STATE_DIR=/root/.local/state/deploy
